278
00:14:04,469 --> 00:14:08,139
then I would say that that is a very poor choice of words.

279
00:14:08,473 --> 00:14:11,851
Michael, he wasn't inferring, he was implying. You were inferring.

280
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:13,353
Was I, Creed?

281
00:14:13,436 --> 00:14:16,814
Okay, well, you know what I am implying

282
00:14:16,898 --> 00:14:21,194
is that when we're on an elevator together, I should maybe take the stairs.

283
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:23,279
Because talk about stank.

284
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:25,823
Not that I would ever say something like that in public,

285
00:14:25,907 --> 00:14:27,658
and I never have, and I never will.

286
00:14:27,742 --> 00:14:31,746
I just think it's something that we should all be aware of, okay?

287
00:14:32,038 --> 00:14:34,999
Now that we've learned this, let's continue.

288
00:14:35,083 --> 00:14:36,084
See, this is good.

289
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:39,045
We're learning and we're figuring some stuff out.

290
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:41,568
"You need to do something about your coffee breath." Okay, no!

291
00:14:41,631 --> 00:14:44,109
"You need to do something..." Shut up, shut up, shut up, Dwight. Okay.

292
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:48,554
I don't think you people are grasping the concept of the suggestion box.

293
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:51,599
Sometimes you talk to us real close. Yeah?

294
00:14:51,933 --> 00:14:54,352
Is that hard for you? All right. Well...

295
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:55,579
Well, when you have coffee breath it's hard...

296
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:56,604
I'll work on that.

297
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:57,980
Okay, let's keep going.

298
00:14:58,064 --> 00:14:59,232
Just keep it going.

299
00:15:00,358 --> 00:15:05,405
Yup. What do we have here? We have somebody's piece of gum.

300
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:09,700
Somebody put a piece of gum in there. This is not a garbage can.

301
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:13,746
This is the future of our company. This is not a place for gum, okay?

302
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:16,249
I don't want to have to read these tomorrow.

303
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,584
Yeah. Who wants to come in on a Saturday?

304
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:21,754
Yeah... What? All right. Next suggestion.

305
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:23,506
"Next suggestion."

306
00:15:25,425 --> 00:15:27,927
"Don't..." Okay, that's blank. Don't... Just...

307
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,763
Put it... "Don't sleep with your boss."

308
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:34,642
Do you think this is referring to you boning Jan?

309
00:15:36,227 --> 00:15:37,579
I can't... I don't understand why you're so upset.

310
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:38,664
I can't... All right, please sit down.

311
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:40,290
I'm going to sit over here, you're gonna sit over there.

312
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,542
Why are you... Let me ask you this.

313
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:43,502
Please sit yourself down. Let me ask you something.

314
00:15:43,526 --> 00:15:45,945
What, Michael? Where did you get your outfit?

315
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:53,035
You're gonna give me this raise. I deserve this raise.

316
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:56,873
Yes! Yes! Yes!

317
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:02,503
The least you can do is keep my salary consistent with inflation.

318
00:16:04,172 --> 00:16:06,924
Yes! Why are you gonna give me this raise?

319
00:16:07,008 --> 00:16:08,134
Why?

320
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:12,388
Because I'm awesome!

321
00:16:12,472 --> 00:16:14,599
I am awesome!

322
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:19,687
I just don't understand why you have to pretend like nothing happened.

323
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,856
Because nothing did, Michael.

324
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:26,986
I'm not gonna say anything more about it and I would advise that you do the same.

325
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:28,446
Look... Michael.

326
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:30,823
Oh, my God. I'm sorry. I'm interrupting. Oh, God.

327
00:16:30,907 --> 00:16:33,701
Were you guys making out? No, Dwight. Come in.

328
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:35,286
Great. What do you want, Dwight?

329
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:37,455
I am ready for my performance review.

330
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,664
Okay, great.

331
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:42,752
Your performance has been adequate. You may leave. Goodbye.

332
00:16:43,753 --> 00:16:46,881
Is this how you've been conducting all the reviews, Michael?

333
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:49,133
Do you want to talk now? Good. Okay, Dwight, leave.

334
00:16:49,217 --> 00:16:51,427
Wait, I would like to discuss my raise.

335
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:54,013
Why on earth would we give you a raise?

336
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:57,391
That is an excellent question. Thank you for asking it.

337
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:02,480
Let me bring up one word. Dedication.

338
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:06,400
I have never been late.

339
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:10,821
Also, I have never missed a day due to illness,

340
00:17:10,905 --> 00:17:13,282
even when I had walking pneumonia.

341
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:15,785
I even come in on holidays.

342
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:17,828
You do? How do you get in?

343
00:17:17,912 --> 00:17:19,539
I have a copy of your key.

344
00:17:19,622 --> 00:17:22,208
That's a serious offense. That is a serious offense.

345
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:23,793
Very serious.

346
00:17:23,918 --> 00:17:25,920
As is toying with a man's heart.

347
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:27,588
Oh, Michael, for God's sakes.

348
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:30,675
I'd also further like to talk about my merits in the workplace.

349
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,344
Okay, third wheel, why don't you do that? For instance,

350
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:35,531
the time I brought in deer jerky for the whole office.

351
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:38,683
That was deer? Gross. Oh, God! - You liked it.

352
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,643
Did not. Jan, have you ever had deer?

353
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:42,186
No. It's a delicacy.

354
00:17:42,270 --> 00:17:44,021
And, you know what? It's an aphrodisiac.

355
00:17:44,105 --> 00:17:45,189
So when we're done here,

356
00:17:45,273 --> 00:17:46,917
you guys could go over to the Antler Lodge,

357
00:17:46,941 --> 00:17:48,734
sample some deer, and talk about my raise.

358
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:50,069
What do you say, Jan?

359
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:51,696
Okay, here's what I'm gonna do.

360
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:53,614
I'm gonna step outside, collect my thoughts,

361
00:17:53,698 --> 00:17:55,449
and I will return in about 10 minutes.

362
00:17:55,533 --> 00:17:58,869
Okay, you just clear your head. Thank you, Dwight.

363
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:01,956
Look, I know it's your job, I know you have to ask,

364
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:04,709
but I promise you I'm not gonna discuss it with him,

365
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:07,128
I'm certainly not gonna discuss it with you.

366
00:18:07,211 --> 00:18:08,879
Do you have a light?

367
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:12,717
And in conclusion, I think Lex Luther said it best when he said,

368
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:15,469
"Dad, you have no idea"

369
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:17,847
"what I'm capable of."

370
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,016
<i>That's from Superman?</i> Smallville.

371
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:24,937
And that is why I feel I deserve this raise.

372
00:18:28,858 --> 00:18:31,402
<i>Do you think Michael and Jan actually...</i>

373
00:18:31,986 --> 00:18:35,239
I don't really wanna picture it. But thank you, Pam.

374
00:18:35,323 --> 00:18:37,116
How do you come back from that?

375
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,410
You don't,

376
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,621
I don't think, come all the way back, you know.

377
00:18:41,704 --> 00:18:43,247
Especially working together.

378
00:18:43,331 --> 00:18:45,333
No, I mean doing that with Michael.

379
00:18:45,416 --> 00:18:48,252
How do you come back from that as a human being?

380
00:18:48,336 --> 00:18:50,671
Yeah. No, I don't think you can.

381
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:53,132
I'm heading back to New York.

382
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:55,801
Alan and I will conduct your performance review

383
00:18:55,885 --> 00:18:56,927
over the phone tomorrow.

384
00:18:57,011 --> 00:18:58,572
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait. Okay? Good.

385
00:18:58,596 --> 00:19:01,599
No, no, no, come... I just want to know why.

386
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:03,809
Michael, now is not the time or the place.

387
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:05,829
Okay, so you're saying that there is a different time or place

388
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:06,913
that we could have this discussion?

389
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:09,398
No. I am saying we are never gonna have this conversation.

390
00:19:09,482 --> 00:19:12,568
Well, okay. What? Never? As in never, ever, ever?

391
00:19:12,652 --> 00:19:14,904
Or never as in there's still a chance?

392
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:17,156
Never for me always means never, ever, ever.

393
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:21,369
I just want to know, from the horse's mouth, what is the dealio?

394
00:19:21,452 --> 00:19:22,846
You know, Michael... Am I too short?

395
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,640
Michael, it has nothing to do with your looks, okay?

396
00:19:24,664 --> 00:19:28,417
It's your personality. I mean, you're obnoxious, and rude,

397
00:19:30,169 --> 00:19:33,673
and stupid, and you do have coffee breath, by the way.

398
00:19:33,756 --> 00:19:36,509
And I don't agree about the B.O.,

399
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:39,595
but you are very, very inconsiderate.

400
00:19:39,929 --> 00:19:42,556
Really? Really. You're...

401
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:44,392
You're a great guy, okay?

402
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:46,102
I appreciate that, thank you.

403
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,603
And you were very sweet.

404
00:19:47,687 --> 00:19:50,564
And you stayed up with me and talked to me

405
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:52,817
and cried with me, and I appreciate that.

406
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,527
No, I didn't. I was... I don't cry.

407
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:58,072
But I just am not in a place right now where I'm looking for a relationship.

408
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:02,368
So, we can still work together, we can still be friends, but...

409
00:20:04,787 --> 00:20:05,871
Okay?

410
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:09,750
So my looks have nothing to do with it?

411
00:20:10,084 --> 00:20:11,585
Oh, God.

412
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:19,635
Jan is not in a place where she feels she can have a relationship right now,

413
00:20:19,719 --> 00:20:22,680
and it doesn't matter how great a guy I am.

414
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,015
And that is all I needed.

415
00:20:25,099 --> 00:20:27,727
I'm good. I can go home now.

416
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,449
Hey, it's 12:20. Where the hell's Dwight?

417
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:43,826
No idea.

418
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:46,036
"Never missed a day," my ass.

419
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:58,466
I'm here! I'm here!

420
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:02,553
I'm here. It's okay!

